<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
"http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.mozilla.prevent-idle-lock</string>
  <!--
    bug 2073762. Hold a PreventUserIdleDisplaySleep assertion for the whole life
    of the task user's GUI session.

    Nothing in a headless worker session ever generates HID input, so
    IOHIDSystem's HIDIdleTime climbs monotonically from console login and is NOT
    reset by task activity (measured on a live m-vms guest: 264 -> 935s while the
    slot was serving tasks). At com.apple.screensaver's default idleTime of 1200s
    the screen saver starts and the session locks; loginwindow becomes frontmost,
    Services.focus.activeWindow goes null, and any harness that waits on a focus
    event hangs until its no-output timeout.

    `pmset displaysleep 0` does NOT cover this -- it stops display sleep, not the
    screen saver. Measured on a guest with displaysleep 0:
    PreventUserIdleDisplaySleep was 0, i.e. no assertion held at all.

    caffeinate is the belt half of belt-and-braces; the braces are the
    -currentHost idleTime 0 write in prevent_idle_lock.pp. The assertion is the
    more reliable of the two because it does not depend on which preference
    domain a given macOS release reads, and -currentHost writes are keyed to the
    hardware UUID (which is what made the image-build write in macos-vms miss).

    -d prevent display idle sleep (this is what suppresses the screen saver)
    -i prevent system idle sleep
    KeepAlive so the assertion is re-established if caffeinate is ever killed.
  -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/caffeinate</string>
    <string>-d</string>
    <string>-i</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
